# Three Blocks (v0.12.x)

Three Blocks is now a public npm package: `npm i three-blocks` (PolyForm
Noncommercial 1.0.0; Pro license for commercial projects). The old private
`@three-blocks/core` package and its CodeArtifact registry are retired — no
`.npmrc` registry entries, login scripts, or `THREE_BLOCKS_SECRET_KEY` are
needed anymore.

Peer dependencies: `three >= 0.185.0`, `vite >= 5.4 < 9`, `stats-gl 4.x`.
WebGPU renderer (`three/webgpu` + TSL) only.

## Import style: per-block subpaths

Everything is imported from `three-blocks/<block>` subpaths (a few symbols are
also re-exported from the root `three-blocks`). Key entry points:

```js
import { SPH } from "three-blocks/sph";
import { PBF } from "three-blocks/pbf";
import { MPMSolver } from "three-blocks/mpm";
import { WaterVolume } from "three-blocks/water";
import { SmokeVolume } from "three-blocks/smoke";
import { GridPristine } from "three-blocks/grid-pristine";
import { MeshTransmissionNodeMaterial } from "three-blocks/transmission";
import { BakedMotion } from "three-blocks/baked-motion";
import { MSDFText, parseMSDFFont } from "three-blocks/msdf-text";
import { ComputeInstanceCulling } from "three-blocks/instance-culling";
import { ComputeMeshSurfaceSampler } from "three-blocks/surface-sampling";
import { SphereImpostorNodeMaterial } from "three-blocks/sphere-impostors";
import { SkinnedMeshSDF } from "three-blocks/sdf-raymarching";
import { defineAssets } from "three-blocks/assets";
import { defineText } from "three-blocks/text";
import { createShaderCache } from "three-blocks/shaders";
import { threeBlocks } from "three-blocks/vite"; // optional vite plugin
import { registerDevtools } from "three-blocks/devtools";
// experimental:
import { GPUInteractionSystem } from "three-blocks/experimental/gpu-interaction";
// also: experimental/vertex-animation-video, experimental/object-animation-video,
// experimental/active-frame-video, experimental/compute-foundations,
// experimental/runtime-sdf-text, boids, gaussian-splats, app, worker, hmr,
// runtime, stats, core-tsl-effects
```

## Removed from the public API (relevant to this repo)

- `GLTFCurveExtension` — replaced by the `defineAssets` pipeline
  (`three-blocks/assets`, `codecs.gltfCurve` / `createCurvePlugin`).
- `AnimationBakeMixer` (VAT) — superseded by Baked Motion
  (`three-blocks/baked-motion`) and the experimental vertex/object animation
  video blocks.

Both compiled modules still ship in `dist/` and this repo aliases them in
`vite.config.js` as `three-blocks-internal/gltf-curve-extension` and
`three-blocks-internal/animation-bake-mixer`. Prefer migrating to the new
APIs over adding more internal aliases.

# Getting Started (starter)

Three Blocks Starter is an officially supported way to create single-page
Three.js applications: `npx create-three-blocks-starter my-app`.

Scripts in this repo: `npm run dev` (vite dev server, port 4000),
`npm run build`, `npm run preview`, `npm run start`. Node 22+ is required by
vite 7 (`nvm use 22`).

## Typical component structure

Components extend the base component helper so they can register themselves
with the shared renderer, scene, and lifecycle events handled off the main
thread.

```js
import * as THREE from 'three/webgpu';
import { component, updateComponentRegistry } from '@/offscreen/dispatcher';
import { scene } from '@/offscreen/main';

export class Component extends component( THREE.Mesh, {
	raf: {
		renderPriority: 1,
		fps: Number.Infinity,
	},
} ) {

	init() {

		// ---- Geometry & Material ----
		this.geometry = new THREE.BoxGeometry( 2, 2, 2 );
		this.material = new THREE.MeshPhysicalNodeMaterial();
		this.material.name = 'ComponentMaterial';

		scene.add( this );

	}

	onDebug( { /* gui */ } ) {}

	onRaf( { /* elapsedTime, delta */ } ) {}
	onResize() {}

	dispose() {

		super.dispose();

	}

}

// Minimal HMR setup
if ( import.meta.hot ) {

	import.meta.hot.accept( ( newModule ) => {

		updateComponentRegistry( 'Component', newModule );

	} );

}
```

Hot Module Replacement (HMR): The starter wires `import.meta.hot.accept()` to
`updateComponentRegistry`, so edits swap in the new class without a full
reload while cleaning up the previous instance.

Global events: The component helper subscribes to shared RAF, resize, and
debug emitters. Implement `onRaf`, `onResize`, and `onDebug` to react to those
global events.

renderPriority & fps: Each component chooses when it should render. Lower
`renderPriority` values update first, and the optional `fps` setting locally
throttles updates so expensive components can run less often.

## Runtime architecture of this repo

- With OffscreenCanvas support (default, no `?debug`), the whole Three.js app
  runs in a worker (`src/offscreen/offscreen.js`) driven from the main thread
  via Comlink; with `?debug` it runs on the main thread.
- Query params are forwarded from the main thread into the worker
  (`setQueryString` in `src/offscreen/lib/query.js`), so `getFlag`/`getParam`
  work in both contexts.
- Useful URL params: `?debug` (main thread + inspector), `?scene=<name|index>`
  (single scene: meadow, demo, vat), `?manual` (disable auto scene cycling),
  `?hidePersistentScene`, `?record`.
- Console helpers (main thread): `gotoScene("demo")`, `gotoScene(2)`,
  `nextScene()`.
